<title>UK: Top UK firms going ex-dividend to impact FTSE 100.</title>
<headline>Top UK firms going ex-dividend to impact FTSE 100.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares going ex-dividend are expected to have a dramatic impact on the FTSE 100 index on Monday 17 March, figures from the London Stock Exchange showed on Thursday.</p>
<p>With eleven members of the elite club trading ex-dividend, including four of the top ten in terms of market capitalisation, the impact will slice around 22 points off the FTSE at the start of trade.</p>
<p>HSBC Holdings Plc, the FTSE 100's largest company in terms of market capitalisation, will alone take around five points off the FTSE.</p>
<p>A list of the shares going ex-dividend and their FTSE 100 ranking in terms of market capitalisation as of the close of business on March 12, 1997 were as follows:</p>
<p>FTSE ranking			Mkt Cap (USD billion) </p>
<p>1. HSBC Holdings PLC			 66.882   </p>
<p>2. Glaxo Wellcome PLC			65.749 </p>
<p>8. Zeneca Group PLC			  28.302 </p>
<p>10.B.A.T. Industries			 27.765  </p>
<p>16.BTR PLC				     18.814   </p>
<p>21.Reuters Holdings			  17.293 </p>
<p>23.RTZ Corp PLC				16.971  </p>
<p>29.Royal and Sun Alliance PLC	    12.358 </p>
<p>42.Cadbury Schweppes PLC		    8.684 </p>
<p>67.GKN PLC					5.877</p>
<p>81.Ladbroke Group PLC			 4.491 </p>
<p> (MARKET CAP SOURCE -- REUTERS SECURITIES 3000)</p>
<p>The following FTSE 100 stocks will go ex-dividend on March 17 and analysts estimate the effect will be to take 22.09 points off the index that day.</p>
<p>					DIVIDEND	INDEX</p>
<p>					(PENCE)	 EFFECT</p>
<p>COMPANY			    Net   Gross    Gross </p>
<p>* BAT Industries		 (a)    20.000   3.620 </p>
<p>* BTR				(b)     7.000   1.638</p>
<p>* Cadbury Schweppes	    11.80  14.750   0.856 </p>
<p>* GKN				16.90  21.125   0.021 </p>
<p>* Glaxo Wellcome		 (c)    22.563   4.670</p>
<p>* HSBC Holdings		  26.00  32.500   1.658 </p>
<p>* HSBC Holdings ($HK)	  26.00  32.500   3.380 </p>
<p>* Ladbroke Group		 3.80    4.750   0.323 </p>
<p>* RTZ Corporation		(d)    23.110   1.433</p>
<p>* Reuters Holdings	     9.00   11.250   1.103 </p>
<p>* Royal &amp; Sun Alliance	 12.50  15.625   1.422 </p>
<p>* Zeneca Group		   22.50  28.125   1.547</p>
<p>(a) For BAT Industries the total dividend amount is 19.5p and includes 17.5p Foreign Income Dividend (FID).</p>
<p>(b) For BTR the dividend is an FID of 7p only.</p>
<p>(c) For Glaxo Wellcome the total dividend amount is 19p and includes an FID of 475p.</p>
<p>(d) For RTZ Corporation the total dividend amount is 13.11p and includes an FID of 21.11p.</p>
